    "svg": "<svg viewBox='0 0 760 444' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' role='img' aria-label='An isotype style chart. A row of grey squares for all developing countries shows a flat dashed arrow and no average growth effect. A row of teal islands shows a rising arrow, a clear positive effect. Beneath, padlocked boxes labelled trade, investment, prices, and country quirks show what the model holds constant.'><rect width='760' height='444' fill='#F6FBFB'/><text x='40' y='40' font-family='Fraunces, Georgia, serif' font-size='19' fill='#0B2530'>Holding the world still</text><text x='40' y='60' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#3D5560'>one panel model, many countries: Feeny, Iamsiraroj and McGillivray, 2014</text><text x='40' y='104' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='10.5' letter-spacing='2' fill='#3D5560'>ALL DEVELOPING COUNTRIES</text><rect x='40' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='65' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='90' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='115' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='140' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='165' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='190' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='215' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='240' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='265' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='290' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='315' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='340' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><rect x='365' y='116' width='18' height='18' rx='4' fill='#8FA6AD' opacity='0.8'/><line x1='555' y1='125' x2='672' y2='125' stroke='#3D5560' stroke-width='2.4' stroke-dasharray='6 5'/><polygon points='670,118 686,125 670,132' fill='#3D5560'/><text x='620' y='152' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>no average growth effect</text><text x='40' y='204' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='10.5' letter-spacing='2' fill='#0E4D5C'>SMALL ISLAND DEVELOPING STATES</text><path d='M39,234 A10,10 0 0 1 59,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M64,234 A10,10 0 0 1 84,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M89,234 A10,10 0 0 1 109,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M114,234 A10,10 0 0 1 134,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M139,234 A10,10 0 0 1 159,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M164,234 A10,10 0 0 1 184,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M189,234 A10,10 0 0 1 209,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M214,234 A10,10 0 0 1 234,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M239,234 A10,10 0 0 1 259,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M264,234 A10,10 0 0 1 284,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M289,234 A10,10 0 0 1 309,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M314,234 A10,10 0 0 1 334,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M339,234 A10,10 0 0 1 359,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><path d='M364,234 A10,10 0 0 1 384,234 Z' fill='#1C8C9B'/><line x1='555' y1='238' x2='672' y2='206' stroke='#1C8C9B' stroke-width='3'/><polygon points='666,200 686,202 674,216' fill='#1C8C9B'/><text x='620' y='260' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0E4D5C'>a clear positive effect,</text><text x='620' y='275' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0E4D5C'>strongest in Africa and the Pacific</text><text x='40' y='306' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='10.5' letter-spacing='2' fill='#3D5560'>WHAT THE MODEL HOLDS STILL</text><rect x='40' y='338' width='96' height='30' rx='6' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#3D5560' stroke-width='1.4'/><text x='88' y='357' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#3D5560'>trade</text><rect x='80' y='326' width='14' height='11' rx='2' fill='#E2664A'/><path d='M83,326 v-4 a4,4 0 0 1 8,0 v4' fill='none' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='1.6'/><rect x='158' y='338' width='96' height='30' rx='6' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#3D5560' stroke-width='1.4'/><text x='206' y='357' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#3D5560'>investment</text><rect x='198' y='326' width='14' height='11' rx='2' fill='#E2664A'/><path d='M201,326 v-4 a4,4 0 0 1 8,0 v4' fill='none' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='1.6'/><rect x='276' y='338' width='96' height='30' rx='6' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#3D5560' stroke-width='1.4'/><text x='324' y='357' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#3D5560'>prices</text><rect x='316' y='326' width='14' height='11' rx='2' fill='#E2664A'/><path d='M319,326 v-4 a4,4 0 0 1 8,0 v4' fill='none' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='1.6'/><rect x='394' y='338' width='96' height='30' rx='6' fill='#FFFFFF' stroke='#3D5560' stroke-width='1.4'/><text x='442' y='357' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11' fill='#3D5560'>country quirks</text><rect x='434' y='326' width='14' height='11' rx='2' fill='#E2664A'/><path d='M437,326 v-4 a4,4 0 0 1 8,0 v4' fill='none' stroke='#993C1D' stroke-width='1.6'/><text x='620' y='352' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>so what remains is the</text><text x='620' y='367' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>remittance effect itself</text><text x='380' y='398' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13' fill='#3D5560'>islands are not small versions of everywhere else; size changes what remittances can do</text><path d='M0,422 C140,415 300,426 460,421 C600,416 690,424 760,420 L760,444 L0,444 Z' fill='#BFE3E2' opacity='0.55'/></svg>",
    "note": "Do remittances make economies grow? Across developing countries as a whole, the study finds essentially no average effect. The interesting result appears when the panel is narrowed to Small Island Developing States: there the association turns positive and significant, and it holds for SIDS in sub-Saharan Africa and the Pacific but not for those in Latin America and the Caribbean. The authors point to the volatility and labour markets of small economies as the reason size changes what money from away can do. The method matters as much as the result. A panel model holds trade, investment, credit, money and each country's quirks still, so that what remains is the remittance association itself, and it is the econometric case that islands are not just small versions of everywhere else.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "t": "Feeny, Iamsiraroj and McGillivray (2014), Remittances and economic growth: larger impacts in smaller countries?, The Journal of Development Studies",
        "u": "https://doi.org/10.1080/00220388.2014.895815"
      }
    ]
