    "svg": "<svg viewBox='0 0 760 384' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' role='img' aria-label='Three houses sit at different depths below a dashed welfare line. The deeper a household sits below the line, the thicker the arrow of remittances reaching it. Above the line, flows still rise with welfare.'><rect width='760' height='384' fill='#F6FBFB'/><text x='40' y='42' font-family='Fraunces, Georgia, serif' font-size='19' fill='#0B2530'>Remittances and the welfare line in Tonga</text><text x='40' y='62' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#3D5560'>how money sent home responds to how households judge</text><text x='40' y='79' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#3D5560'>their own welfare, from a customised household survey in Tonga</text><line x1='70' y1='330' x2='70' y2='106' stroke='#D7E6E6' stroke-width='2'/><polygon points='66,112 70,102 74,112' fill='#D7E6E6'/><text x='58' y='218' transform='rotate(-90 58 218)' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='10' letter-spacing='2' fill='#3D5560'>WELLBEING</text><line x1='100' y1='196' x2='700' y2='196' stroke='#E2664A' stroke-width='2' stroke-dasharray='7 6'/><text x='400' y='182' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#993C1D'>the line households draw themselves, enough to get by</text><text x='648' y='118' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>above the line, money</text><text x='648' y='132' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>keeps rising with welfare</text><path d='M612,166 C630,156 650,150 672,146 L676,145' stroke='#1C8C9B' stroke-width='1.8' fill='none'/><polygon points='672,139 684,143 674,151' fill='#1C8C9B'/><line x1='200' y1='206' x2='200' y2='262' stroke='#1C8C9B' stroke-width='7'/><polygon points='190,260 200,276 210,260' fill='#1C8C9B'/><polygon points='170,300 200,276 230,300' fill='#1C8C9B'/><rect x='178' y='300' width='44' height='30' fill='#1C8C9B'/><line x1='430' y1='206' x2='430' y2='230' stroke='#1C8C9B' stroke-width='4'/><polygon points='422,228 430,244 438,228' fill='#1C8C9B'/><polygon points='400,268 430,244 460,268' fill='#1C8C9B'/><rect x='408' y='268' width='44' height='30' fill='#1C8C9B'/><line x1='630' y1='202' x2='630' y2='214' stroke='#1C8C9B' stroke-width='2'/><polygon points='624,212 630,226 636,212' fill='#1C8C9B'/><polygon points='600,250 630,226 660,250' fill='#1C8C9B'/><rect x='608' y='250' width='44' height='30' fill='#1C8C9B'/><text x='380' y='352' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13.5' fill='#3D5560'>below the line, remittances rise as need deepens, social protection sent from abroad</text><path d='M0,368 C140,361 300,372 460,367 C600,362 690,369 760,366 L760,384 L0,384 Z' fill='#BFE3E2' opacity='0.55'/></svg>",
    "note": "Using a customised household survey in Tonga, the study asks what remittances respond to. Below a welfare line that households define themselves, money sent home behaves like social protection, rising as need deepens, which the authors read as evidence supportive of altruism toward the poorest. Above that line remittances keep rising with welfare, closer to an exchange between family members than a safety net. The effect of remittances on poverty and inequality is therefore more layered than a single average suggests.",
