    "svg": "<svg viewBox='0 0 760 350' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' role='img' aria-label='Two equal bars show that people receiving remittances are as likely to work as people who do not. Beside them, arrows show what shifts instead: informal work and self employment rise while wage work falls.'><rect width='760' height='350' fill='#F6FBFB'/><text x='40' y='42' font-family='Fraunces, Georgia, serif' font-size='19' fill='#0B2530'>Remittances and the shape of work in Comoros</text><text x='40' y='62' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#3D5560'>households receiving money from abroad beside households that do not,</text><text x='40' y='79' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='12.5' fill='#3D5560'>national household surveys of 2014 and 2020</text><text x='220' y='118' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='11' letter-spacing='2' fill='#3D5560'>WHO WORKS</text><rect x='130' y='170' width='60' height='110' fill='#1C8C9B' fill-opacity='0.92' stroke='#0E4D5C' stroke-width='2'/><rect x='250' y='170' width='60' height='110' fill='none' stroke='#1C8C9B' stroke-width='2'/><text x='220' y='234' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Fraunces, Georgia, serif' font-size='30' fill='#0B2530'>=</text><line x1='110' y1='282' x2='330' y2='282' stroke='#D7E6E6' stroke-width='2'/><text x='160' y='300' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>receive</text><text x='280' y='300' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>do not receive</text><line x1='380' y1='110' x2='380' y2='300' stroke='#D7E6E6' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-dasharray='4 5'/><text x='570' y='118' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Space Mono, monospace' font-size='11' letter-spacing='2' fill='#3D5560'>WHAT WORK LOOKS LIKE</text><text x='470' y='164' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0E4D5C'>more</text><line x1='470' y1='268' x2='470' y2='190' stroke='#1C8C9B' stroke-width='6'/><polygon points='460,194 470,176 480,194' fill='#1C8C9B'/><text x='570' y='164' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#0E4D5C'>more</text><line x1='570' y1='268' x2='570' y2='190' stroke='#1C8C9B' stroke-width='6'/><polygon points='560,194 570,176 580,194' fill='#1C8C9B'/><text x='670' y='164' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#993C1D'>less</text><line x1='670' y1='190' x2='670' y2='258' stroke='#E2664A' stroke-width='6'/><polygon points='660,254 670,272 680,254' fill='#E2664A'/><line x1='420' y1='282' x2='720' y2='282' stroke='#D7E6E6' stroke-width='2'/><text x='470' y='300' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>informal work</text><text x='570' y='300' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>self employment</text><text x='670' y='300' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='11.5' fill='#3D5560'>wage work</text><text x='380' y='326' text-anchor='middle' font-family='Spline Sans, sans-serif' font-size='13.5' fill='#3D5560'>remittances did not pull Comorians out of work, they changed the work people do</text><path d='M0,338 C140,332 300,342 460,337 C600,333 690,340 760,336 L760,350 L0,350 Z' fill='#BFE3E2' opacity='0.55'/></svg>",
    "note": "Comoros receives the second largest flow of remittances in Africa as a share of its economy. Matching individuals in households that receive money from relatives away, at home or abroad, against matched individuals in households that do not, across the 2014 and 2020 national surveys, the study finds no evidence of idleness on average. Receivers are as likely to take part in the labour market, and the authors report that remittances move neither unemployment nor hours worked. Above a threshold this changes, and the households receiving the largest transfers do take part less. What changes for everyone else is the kind of work, because receivers are more likely to be in informal work and, on the 2014 figures, more likely to be self employed and less likely to hold a wage job.",
